iplinary Potential of Pure Sociology]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>Last year I published this piece in The American Sociologist as part of a special issue on the sociology and legacy of Donald Black. You can view the official version here, if you can get past the paywall. I, ironically, cannot. I reproduce a slightly edited version below. These are my most ambitious ideas so far, and therefore most likely to be wrong. …</p><p>URL: <a href="https://jasonmanning.substack.com/p/the-interdisciplinary-potential-of?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://jasonmanning.substack.com/p/the-interdisciplinary-potential-of?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/psychology-links-742026">Psychology Links, 7/4/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://jasonmanning.substack.com/p/the-interdisciplinary-potential-of?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://jasonmanning.substack.com/p/the-interdisciplinary-potential-of?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 11:03:29 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>